Package: dmlrs
Type: Package
Title: Fast Double / Debiased Machine Learning Implemented in 'Rust'
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Asad", "Gudzevic", email = "asadgudzevic94@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Authors of the bundled Rust crates", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "see inst/AUTHORS")
  )
Description: Double / debiased machine learning (Chernozhukov et al. (2018)
    <doi:10.1111/ectj.12097>) for causal inference: partially linear,
    interactive, instrumental variable, difference-in-differences (including
    staggered adoption) and regression discontinuity models with cross-fitted
    nuisance functions, multiplier bootstrap and sensitivity analysis for
    omitted confounding, plus heterogeneous effects (best linear predictor,
    meta-learners, causal forests, conformal intervals), dose-response curves,
    causal mediation, effects on censored time-to-event outcomes, difference in
    differences with a continuous treatment, synthetic difference in
    differences, optimal policy trees, Lee bounds, anytime-valid confidence
    sequences for monitoring a study and prediction-powered inference from a
    few labels and many predictions. Estimation runs in parallel in 'Rust'
    through the 'dml-core' crate, including the nuisance learners: least
    absolute shrinkage and selection operator (lasso) regression, logistic
    regression, random forests and gradient boosting. Results match the
    'Python' package 'dml-rs', which is validated against 'DoubleML'.
